# 3. Elevation Layer Alignment & Guardrails
- Layer rule: {{SUB_REPO_NAME}} MUST not call on-prem data center endpoints directly.
- Allowed upstream access: only via declared gateways: {{UPSTREAM_DEPENDENCIES}} or Sentient-OS global API gateway at {{GLOBAL_API_GATEWAY_URL}}.
- Egress enforcement:
  - All outgoing HTTP/gRPC calls must pass through service discovery / API gateway.
  - All events published must use the central topic prefix: sentient.<layer>.<service>.
- Required headers for telemetry and governance:
  - X-SENTIENT-REQ-ID: UUID v4
  - X-SENTIENT-SERVICE: {{SUB_REPO_NAME}}
  - X-SENTIENT-ENV: {{ENV}}
  - X-SENTIENT-TIME: ISO8601 UTC
- Secrets & auth:
  - Secrets must use central secret manager (vault path: {{VAULT_PATH}}).
  - No hard-coded credentials in repo.

# 4. Contract Versioning & Compatibility Rules
- Versioning: SemVer enforced for all contract IDs.
- Breaking change = MAJOR version bump.
- Minor/patch allowed for additive or non-breaking fixes.
- Consumer must support at least two previous minor versions where possible.

# 5. Contract Breaking-Change Checklist
- For each downstream consumer in {{DOWNSTREAM_CONSUMERS}}:
  - [ ] Notify consumer owners 30 days prior for MAJOR changes.
  - [ ] Create migration guide with sample requests/responses.
  - [ ] Provide feature flag or dual-write support for 90-day overlap.
  - [ ] Add automated compatibility tests in CI that run against downstream mock harnesses.
  - [ ] Publish updated OpenAPI/AsyncAPI and schema to registry.
- Local checklist to run before pushing MAJOR:
  - [ ] Bump contract version in schema files.
  - [ ] Run schema compliance tests (see Section 6).
  - [ ] Run cross-repo contract linter.
  - [ ] Open PR with clear Contract-Change label and link to consumers affected.
  - [ ] Schedule contract verification run with Platform team.

# 6. CI/CD: Schema Verification & Gates
- Pre-merge checks:
  - Step 1: Validate local schema files against Sentient-OS schema lint rules (tool: spectral/jsonschema) — command: {{CMD_SCHEMA_LINT}}
  - Step 2: Run contract verifier that queries central registry for current contract versions — command: {{CMD_VERIFY_REGISTRY}}
  - Step 3: Run consumer compatibility tests (mocks) — command: {{CMD_RUN_COMPAT_TESTS}}
  - Step 4: Run unit and integration tests.
- Merge gate:
  - Fail merge if schema lint or registry validation fails.
  - Require "contract-review" approval from Platform or owning team for MAJOR bumps.
- Release:
  - On publish, push schemas to central registry at {{REGISTRY_URL}} with metadata: service, commit, version, checksum.

